WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:02.221
Now apply the same design process to

00:00:02.234 --> 00:00:07.006
a bookstore Start by identifying candidate entities

00:00:07.033 --> 00:00:09.848
such as customer book author order and

00:00:09.875 --> 00:00:13.974
order item Then define one-row grain for

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:19.310
each table Think about the relationships One

00:00:19.337 --> 00:00:22.916
customer can place many orders One order

00:00:22.942 --> 00:00:26.087
can contain many books One book can

00:00:26.113 --> 00:00:29.192
have several authors which suggests another
many-to-many

00:00:29.218 --> 00:00:33.919
relationship Choose stable primary keys and protect

00:00:33.946 --> 00:00:36.617
important natural identifiers such as email or

00:00:36.630 --> 00:00:41.197
ISBN when appropriate Before revealing the sample

00:00:41.223 --> 00:00:43.999
direction create your own simple design first

00:00:45.750 --> 00:00:47.447
There can be more than one reasonable

00:00:47.460 --> 00:00:49.750
implementation but every table should have a

00:00:49.763 --> 00:00:51.815
clear grain and every relationship should be

00:00:51.842 --> 00:00:53.434
explainable in plain language
